# Keep the build context to what the Dockerfile actually copies.
#
# Correctness first: `data/` holds a node's private key, its database and its tenants'
# content. It is gitignored, so it never reaches a commit — but a build context is not a
# commit, and without this line a developer building locally would send their key to the
# daemon and, with a careless `COPY . .`, into a layer of a published image.
data/
deploy/secrets/
.env
*.env

.git/
.github/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

tests/
migrations/versions/__pycache__/
